WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:04.540
BIue Moon has the meaning of
an "impossible proposition".

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.960
It is a cocktail feared by all men
trying to pick up women in bars.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.180
Five different types of Pastis.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:45.890
I will now arrange them in order and ask
you to taste and name each one of them.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.350
Make a single mistake
and I will be the winner.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:50.940
In other words,

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.690
if you insist on
comparing me to a Pastis,

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.570
which has the meaning of an "imitation",

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.070
then you may give me no wrong answers.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.740
Because, ultimately,
the fate of one woman depends

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.620
on the outcome of this duel.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.350
Very well. I will now turn around.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.310
PIease order the glasses as you wish.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.770
Bartender, Ryu Sasakura,
thinks the following...

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.820
The bar counter is like a tiny stage.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.950
Here, little white lies may be forgiven.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.200
One's age, profession, history...

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:49.830
Even "love" may be included.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:56.800
However, for him, there is one thing
that people should never lie about.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:02.130
For instance, a ring that has been
placed between two people.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:07.770
A sparkle of temptation that would destroy

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.430
a woman's most beautiful memories.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.230
The name of that ring's owner is...

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.900
Masahiro Oda.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:16.610
His profession...

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.440
con artist.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.150
That's right.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:23.320
Deceiving people with sneaky lies
is how I make a living.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.910
And tonight I am going to
use false love to swipe money

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:30.870
from this unsuspecting young lady.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.460
But before that...

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.130
I have to get past this bartender.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.380
When did he figure out
that I was a con man?

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.880
I need to get past this hurdle first.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:48.430
What a lovely bar.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.060
Yeah, I only recently discovered it.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.770
They call this bartender here,
"The GIass of the Gods", you know.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.610
I've been coming here
the Iast few days. Right?

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:58.690
Indeed.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:03.280
Dr Oda drinks very smartly
and is a very good patron.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:07.160
There you go again with the flattery.
You're hoping for a tip, perhaps?

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:08.330
Not at all.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:10.750
Well, then...

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.710
In that case, I would like to present
the lovely couple here

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:15.250
with a tip from the heart.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.210
We begin with cacao liqueur.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.050
Then float a little cream on the surface.

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:29.010
The trick here is to keep
the cream's texture very thin.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.470
And last but not least.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.350
Angel's Tip.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:36.350
Is what we call this one.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.110
What a romantic cocktail.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:41.150
Indeed.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.610
But in Japan it has another name.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:45.990
The Angel's Kiss.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:46.910
Kiss?

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:51.490
Try sliding the cherry along the toothpick
and then dipping it into the glass.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.290
Like this?

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.330
Now, when you pull it out
from the drink, slowly...

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.260
-The cocktail's moving!
-The cocktail's moving!

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.590
And are those...?

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:11.060
Quite. It looks like a pair of lips,
doesn't it?

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.270
Hence the name, "Angel's Kiss".

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:15.140
A kiss from an Angel, you say...

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:16.480
Isn't it just...

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:18.400
so cute.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:22.480
The Angel's Kiss...

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:24.490
As expected from the Glass of the Gods.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.280
Thanks to you her guard
is completely down.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:28.410
So...

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.530
What will you be having, sir?

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.120
Oh, right.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.540
I'll have an old rum or cognac. Straight.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.830
How about a Lapalun, then?

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:42.090
The maturity of this old rum
makes it a delicious little tipple.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.090
I'll have one of those then.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:51.100
Hey. You often see that wrapper
on old bottles in bars, am I right?

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:53.350
Indeed. We call it parafilm.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:58.690
It is highly elasticated and can stick to
and seal any shape bottle.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.730
Say, I couldn't have a strip could I?

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:02.440
Certainly.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:05.190
It's so springy!

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:09.070
Man, they sure do think of
everything these days.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:13.740
Surely not. Was it then?

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:18.160
No... That was just something
to keep the mood light.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:21.920
But then, what else could it be...?

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:23.880
Oh no...

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.960
What time is it now?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.800
Sorry, miss.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:30.680
We don't keep clocks in bars.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:35.510
Right. 'Cause here we forget what time
it is and enjoy a slow drink...

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.270
But, I...

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.520
have to be home by midnight.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:40.730
It's fine.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.770
There's still time left. See?

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.650
Whoa. What a nice watch!

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.410
This guy was Ieft to me by my grandfather
who lost his life in the war.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.540
But every now and then it's okay
to forget about the time when drinking.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:58.290
Right.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.330
But... I'm sorry.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.370
I need to get back by 12.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.210
Don't worry about it.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:07.550
I know your parents are strict
with that curfew.

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:08.840
First off,

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:11.590
if it turned out that it was
my fault you broke curfew,

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.850
I'd be in real hot water with
your father when he meets me.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:18.220
Okay. I guess we'd better get going.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:20.730
Sorry for always being
such boring customers.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:23.440
Hospital wages aren't that great,

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.020
so I can't go ordering expensive drinks.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:28.190
Please, don't worry about that.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:34.820
Take care.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.870
My preparation was flawless.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:44.420
All that remained was
for me to pull off my lie,

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:46.250
at this bar counter.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:50.210
I'm a bit early, do you mind?

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:51.720
Not at all. PIease come in.

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:53.800
Thanks for the last time.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:57.550
She really enjoyed that Angel's Kiss,

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:00.310
so she asked to come back here.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.480
We've got a rendezvous tonight.

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:04.560
The one annoyance is that

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:07.820
her carriage turns into a pumpkin
unless she gets home by midnight.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:11.320
But today's the day I chance my arm...

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:14.610
Is that a ring, perchance?

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.740
Are you planning on
proposing to her at our bar?

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.740
You don't mind, do you?

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:20.700
In fact.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.250
I would rather you didn't.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:26.000
Propose to her, I mean.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.340
Hey, hey.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:31.340
What's got into you?

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:32.550
I believe...

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:35.010
you know best why I say that, sir.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:37.090
What's your deal, man?

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.430
If you really don't understand,

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:42.730
please try this.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.360
What the hell kind of drink is that?

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:52.690
It tastes Iike a cross between mint
toothpaste and Chinese five spice.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.570
The flavour almost set my tongue on fire.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:00.280
You just tried a "Pernod".

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.620
Nine out of ten customers who try it
pull a face of disgust.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:07.120
The remaining ten percent
become die-hard fans.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.790
You're telling me there are people
who drink this stuff willingly?

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.920
Did you know that there is a type
of liqueur they call "Pastis"?

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:18.090
No. My knowledge of spirits
is non-existent.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:21.970
In France, they have
a famous spirit called Absinthe.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:24.850
However, because it contained
ingredients deemed

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:26.940
dangerous to one's health,
such as wormwood,

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.480
it was banned 100 years ago.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:32.690
And so, as a replacement,

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:36.320
they created pastis,
with aniseed as its base.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.570
It comes from the word "pastiche".

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:40.450
Meaning, in French,

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:42.200
to imitate.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.000
Imitate?

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.580
Or, to copy. As in a fake?

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.800
Yes. You, yourself, are a fake, sir.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.300
In other words, a con man.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:57.880
Correct.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:01.930
And, with this ring, you intend
to complete your con.

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:03.600
With a fake proposal.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:05.180
That was the plan.

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:08.440
I'm sorry,

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:11.360
but I will have to ask you to refrain
from doing that here.

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.320
A con man, eh?

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:14.980
And what evidence do you have?

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:16.490
You're right.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.360
I have no evidence.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:19.910
But...

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:21.530
Do you know

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:26.080
what it is that bartenders serve
customers on this bar counter?

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:27.500
Lipuor, right?

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:29.540
No. That is incorrect.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:31.580
We serve good memories.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:32.920
A relaxing time.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:34.590
CIeansing of the soul.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:37.130
The bar counter

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:39.680
is a stage where all
those memories are gathered.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:43.550
For that purpose,
we do allow certain white lies.

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:46.970
Age, profession, personal history.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:48.850
Even love.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:50.850
But...

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:54.860
there is one lie that
a bartender cannot forgive.

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:57.940
That is to say.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:59.610
An ugly lie

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:03.990
that might destroy what would otherwise
be a lady's most precious memory,

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.120
here at the bar.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:14.630
You're funny.

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.250
You're a funny dude!

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.670
You call me a con man,
without a shred of evidence.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.260
And try to kick me out.

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:23.090
You think I care about your Pastis?

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.550
You think I care about
your "ugly lie" at the bar?

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:29.600
Fine.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:33.690
I'll play along and
admit that I'm a con man...

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:37.860
If you can beat me at this duel!

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:39.690
Duel?

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:44.110
A duel?

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:45.120
Right.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:47.030
You compared me to this pastis,

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:49.160
and said I'm a fake, didn't you?

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:52.000
You must be pretty
confident at sniffing out lies.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:53.620
What's this about?

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:55.330
Just a little bar game.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.050
How many types of pastis do you have here?

00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:59.340
Five.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:01.510
Fine, I'll have one of each.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.010
Okay. I've got you now.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.600
He's not so confident anymore.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:12.180
Pernod. Ricard. Pastis.

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:13.730
Pastis 51 .

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.650
Berger BIanc.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:18.190
Is this a taste test?

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:20.780
Yep. I wonder if you'll get them all.

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:22.030
There's one problem.

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:25.610
Bartenders may not
get drunk whilst at work.

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:28.160
Is that how you want get out of this?

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:31.040
We'd better hurry before she gets here.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:32.660
In that case...

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.260
Let's put only
a single drop into this water.

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.510
There's no chance
I'll get drunk, that way.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:44.550
Huh!

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:47.430
You're confident you'll be able
to tell just with one drop?

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:48.220
I am.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:52.140
Yeah, right. Like my lies are
that easy to see through...

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:53.680
Fine by me.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:56.190
But if you lose,

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.900
I'll be Iooking for an apology.

00:12:58.150 --> 00:12:58.810
Of course.

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:00.980
But if I win,

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:02.280
If you win...?

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:05.280
How about telling a beautiful lie?

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:06.820
A beautiful lie?

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:08.320
For instance,

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:11.540
five parts mineral water
to one part pastis.

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:12.870
And ice.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:18.000
This Pastis 51 has both the meaning of
having been created in 1951 ,

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:21.590
and that the ratio of water to alcohol
should be 5 to 1 .

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:31.010
The colour changed to a milky white!

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:34.100
Please, enjoy this Pastis water.

00:13:36.890 --> 00:13:39.020
Now this is easy on the palate.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:41.320
Far more delicious
than drinking it straight.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:43.690
In Provence, in the south of France,

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.400
pastis has the meaning of "mixing".

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:51.660
That is because mixing
pastis with water is the norm.

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:53.700
Then we have Turkish Raki,

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.040
and Ouzo from Greece.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:58.580
There are a great many other
spirits that turn cloudy white.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:13:59.920
And they all do this

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:02.790
because the oils which have dissolved in
the strong alcohol,

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:06.590
begin to show as the water dilutes them.

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:07.880
How strange.

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:11.090
Who knew there were spirits that
change colour when water is added.

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:14.140
There are many types of spirit whose
expression, colour

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:17.980
or way of drinking are not
always visible on the surface.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:20.520
What are you trying to say?

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:25.900
That I believe there might be a certain
kindness hidden within a Iie.

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.530
Even demons have hearts, you mean?

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:29.450
Not quite.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:30.780
I just mean...

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.530
rather than hurting the young lady
who will soon be arriving,

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:37.290
the memories she has of this place
could stay beautiful.

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:40.120
Is that your "beautiful lie"?

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:42.750
I see. Not bad...

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.750
He's coming back at me
with psychological warfare, then?

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:47.510
Well...

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:50.720
it looks like you're intent on
making me out to be a con man,

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:53.260
so, if you win...

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:54.890
In which case...

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:59.680
That's right. Go on then!

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:01.690
Each and every drop...

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:03.520
will be your very undoing!

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.650
Now then. I will turn around.

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:09.650
PIease order the glasses as you wish.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.370
You dolt.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:16.660
It makes no difference how
I rearrange these glasses,

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:20.290
you will have the advantage,
being a bartender...

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:27.500
Then, why would I knowingly
set up such a challenge...?

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:31.050
That itself was
the very beginning of my Iie.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:39.980
Okay, ready when you are.

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:41.310
Alright.

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:43.520
What's this?

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:45.980
That look...
It's like he's a different person.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:51.150
It's no surprise he saw
straight through me.

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:54.240
Let's see what you've got, then.

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:55.660
I'll begin.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:15:59.580
Pernod.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:00.750
Huh.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.620
Next then.

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:08.340
Ricard. Then we have Pastis.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:10.300
And then Pastis 51 .

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:13.050
Pretty impressive.

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:15.760
Which means that the last one must be...

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:16.800
Hang on!

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:20.720
I want to ask you one thing
before the last glass.

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:24.140
Why did you think I was a con man?

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:27.730
Instead of saying three ugly truths,

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:29.900
it's better to say a beautiful lie.

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:31.110
Well, well.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:34.150
I didn't expect to find a bartender
who could quote Rabelais.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:35.410
Well?

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:37.780
Firstly, your watch from the other day.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:38.990
My watch?

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:42.830
It's fine.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:44.830
There's still time left. See.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.670
Whoa! What a nice watch.

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:49.590
At that time,

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:53.220
you said the watch had belonged
to your grandfather who died at war.

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:55.220
But that would be strange.

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:58.640
Reason being, that is a quartz watch.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.640
And the quartz watch only came about

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:03.810
in 1969.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:07.190
There is no way it could
have belonged to your grandfather.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:09.360
That's some good eyes you've got.

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:12.530
Seems to me you're more observant
than even a con artist.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:15.740
It's almost pathological
for a bartender's eyes

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:18.910
to go to a customer's hand
as it Iays on the counter.

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:23.700
The seconds hand moves differently on a
quartz watch compared to a mechanical one.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.040
But that's still not proof.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:28.880
Then there was the parafilm incident.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:32.550
It was originally used
to hermetically seal samples

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:34.090
in test tubes and petri dishes.

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:37.590
A man of medicine never having heard of it

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:40.510
is like a bartender never
having heard of a shaker.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:43.220
And you had this confirmed by a doctor?

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:43.970
I did.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:45.140
I see.

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:46.730
The watch, the film...

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:49.980
And what is the third ugly truth?

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:51.110
That is...

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:53.780
That is...

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:55.280
A secret conversation.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:56.700
A secret conversation?

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.280
Please take care.

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:04.580
I only need 3 million yen.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.410
The funds for my clinic have run dry.

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:10.540
What? That's impossible.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.840
You heard that hushed conversation?

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:14.420
There's more.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:24.180
More?

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:26.020
Oh, nothing.

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:28.850
At any rate, there is only
one reason that someone Iike you,

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:31.810
who isn't a doctor,
should propose to a woman

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:34.320
after asking her
to Iend you so much money.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.610
I see. Which is why
I got given that pastis.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:38.990
An imitation, a con man...

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:41.110
Okay. I get it.

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:42.950
Let's get this over with.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:43.780
Agreed.

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:46.330
Now then, am I truly a con man?

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:50.920
Well, what do you think?

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:53.170
What do two Iies
mixed together taste like?

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:57.050
Berger BIanc...

00:18:57.380 --> 00:18:59.170
Got you! I win!

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:01.260
Mixed with Pernod.

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:02.970
What?

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:04.550
How did you...?

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:09.390
You're telling me you managed to taste
the two different alcohols mixed together?

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:11.900
I am a bartender, after all.

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.040
The Glass of the Gods, eh?

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:31.870
I suppose I'll just have to accept defeat.

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:35.090
I guess you can't get
anything past a bartender.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:38.130
Yes?

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:39.760
Hello.

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:42.880
This is Oda.
I've got something to tell you...

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.930
Okay. Sure.

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:47.140
I understand. Take care.

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:50.930
Thank you very much.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:52.890
Come on then. Let's go home.

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:56.020
Sorry, baby.

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:59.190
I still haven't found you a new daddy.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:00.650
But...

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:03.530
at least your mum
didn't become a liar.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:14.620
Cinderella.

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.170
Her real identity after the magic wore off

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.170
was a single mother
who loves her daughter.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:22.630
And...

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:25.800
the bartender not only managed
to unveil the con man's true form,

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:30.180
but allowed the couple to keep their lies.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:34.020
Three lies sparkling in Ginza.

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:35.730
The first,

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:37.860
the con man's beautiful lie.

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:39.360
The second,

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:42.990
the beautiful lie told by
a loving mother for her daughter.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:44.610
And,

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:46.570
the third.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.410
For the bartender,

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:51.240
this bar counter is a very special place.

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.080
If at all possible,

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.670
it is preferable to adorn it,
not with ugly lies,

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:58.130
but with beautiful ones.

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:13.890
RECIPE: PASTIS 51 - 40ml
MINERAL WATER - 120ml

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:31.140
Project supervisor: Justine Cocquyt
Spotting: Capucine Cocquyt

